  "_pathNote": "`path` is the exact road polyline the bus drives, as surveyed coordinates [lat,lng]. When present it overrides straight lines between stops, and the tracker measures progress along it. MBH uses a one-way loop: the outbound and return trips take different roads, so mbh_to_east and east_to_mbh are NOT reverses of each other.",
  "_pathProvenance": "mbh_to_east / east_to_mbh: hand-surveyed GPS points. ac_mbh_out / ac_arch_to_mbh: sliced from those surveys. LH and SOMS routes: traced along OpenStreetMap road geometry through supplied waypoints, with the ATM-Circle-to-East-Campus stretch spliced from the hand survey. The final ~250 m into SOMS is a straight line because no road to SOMS is mapped in OSM."
}
